{
  "_about": "How technical terms are said aloud. narrate looks for each key of \"terms\" in a scene's \"say\" (as a whole word, exact case) and speaks its value, while the caption shows the term as written. In a dotted name such as Render.fs or window.render the dot is said \"dot\" and each part is said by \"terms\", else by \"extensions\" (the part in lower case), else as written. A repository's own .codebase-video/glossary.json has the same shape and is laid over this one: its entries win, and an empty string leaves a term as written. A [shown](spoken) in the script wins over both.",
